{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "kind": "help-article",
  "title": "Configuring Scan Rule for AWS Virtual Machines",
  "source": {
    "url": "https://help.zscaler.com/ai-asset-mgmt/configuring-scan-rule-aws-virtual-machines",
    "node": "1540275",
    "revision": "3202211",
    "updated": "2026-06-06",
    "updated_basis": "pdf-last-modified"
  },
  "captured_at": "2026-11-04",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "text": "You can configure the scan rule to scan Amazon Web Services (AWS) virtual machines. AI Security scans the EC2 instances for any sensitive data."
    },
    {
      "text": "You can configure the scan rule after onboarding the AWS accounts. To learn more, see About Cloud Accounts."
    },
    {
      "text": "To configure a scan rule for AWS virtual machines, complete the following steps in the AI Security Admin Portal:"
    },
    {
      "item": "1. Provide the general information.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Go to Administration > Scan Settings.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          20
        ],
        [
          23,
          36
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Select the Scan Rules tab.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          11,
          21
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "If you are configuring the scan rule for the first time, the following page appears:",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Add Scan Rule.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          19
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "The General Information page appears.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          4,
          23
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "On the General Information page:",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 4,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          26
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Scan Rule Name: Enter a unique and descriptive name for the scan rule.",
      "depth": 2,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          14
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Scan Rule Description (Optional): Enter a description for the scan rule (maximum is 500 characters).",
      "depth": 2,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          32
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Next.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 5,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "2. Select the cloud and resource type.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Select Cloud and Resource Type page:",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          37
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "For Cloud Type, select AWS.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          4,
          14
        ],
        [
          23,
          26
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "For Resource Type, select Virtual Machine.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          4,
          17
        ],
        [
          26,
          41
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Next.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "3. Select the accounts that must be scanned.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Select Resources to Scan page, select one of the following options:",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          31
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Scan All Resources: Scans all the virtual machines across all onboarded accounts.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          18
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 2
    },
    {
      "item": "Scan Specific Resources: Scan only specific accounts. When you select this option, select the checkbox for the accounts that must be scanned.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          23
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Select Specific Accounts and Regions: Select the checkbox for specific accounts and regions that must be scanned.",
      "depth": 3,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          36
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Scan Specific Instances: Specify the virtual machines that must be scanned.",
      "depth": 3,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          23
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Select from the List: Select the checkbox for the instances that must be scanned from the list. If you choose Manual, enter the instance ARNs separated by commas.",
      "depth": 4,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          20
        ],
        [
          110,
          116
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Select by Tags: Enter the key-value pairs for the instances. All the instances that match the tag are scanned. Click Add More to add multiple key-value pairs.",
      "depth": 4,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          14
        ],
        [
          117,
          125
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "If multiple key-value pairs are added, AI Security scans all instances that match at least one of the specified key-value pairs. This means the rule uses OR logic, and a instance is included if it matches any of the key-value pairs.",
      "depth": 4
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 2
    },
    {
      "item": "If you chose Scan All Resources, or Scan Specific Resources, you can optionally exclude some VMs from the scan.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          13,
          31
        ],
        [
          36,
          59
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Enable Malware Scanning: Enable this option if the resources must be scanned for malware. This option is disabled by default.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          23
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Next.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "4. Exclude virtual machines (Optional).",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Exclude Virtual Machines (Optional) page, you can specify the VMs that must be excluded from the scan.",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          42
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Enter the EC2 VM names separated by commas.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Exclude Virtual Machines By Tags: Enable this option and enter the key-value pairs of the VMs that must be excluded from scanning. This option is disabled by default. Click Add More to add multiple key-value pairs.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          32
        ],
        [
          173,
          181
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "If multiple key-value pairs are added, AI Security excludes any VMs that matches at least one of the specified key-value pairs. This means the rule uses OR logic, and a VM is excluded if it matches any of the key-value pairs.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Exclude Operating System Directories Files from Scanning: Disable this option if you want to scan the OS directories. This option is enabled by default.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          56
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "The following directories are excluded from the scan:",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Linux",
      "depth": 2
    },
    {
      "item": "/usr/local/",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "/usr/lib/",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "/usr/lib64/",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "/usr/share/",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "/usr/bin/",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "/usr/sbin/",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "/usr/src/",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "/usr/include/",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "/usr/libexec/",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "/var/app/",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "/var/log/",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "/var/lib/",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "/var/cache/",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "/etc/",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "/boot/",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "Windows",
      "depth": 2
    },
    {
      "item": "C:\\Program Files\\",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "C:\\Windows\\",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "Packages",
      "depth": 2
    },
    {
      "item": "/smui/",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "/smca/",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "/opt/elasticbeanstalk/",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Next.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 4,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "5. Set up the scan schedule.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Scan Schedule page, select the scan frequency:",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          20
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "On Demand (Default): Scan the data manually when needed.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          9
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Daily: Scan the data daily.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          5
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Weekly: Scan the data once a week. Select the day from the drop-down menu.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          6
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Monthly: Scan the data once a month.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          7
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Next.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "6. Select the scan scope.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Scan Scope page, choose a scan scope from the drop-down menu to set up your scan rule.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          17
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "To learn more about configuring and creating a scan scope, see Configuring Scan Scope.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Next.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "7. Review and complete the configuration.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Review the scan rule. Click the Edit icon to change any values, if required.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          32,
          36
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Finish.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          12
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}
